    "summary": "Fresh plan-only ACCEPT. I-18.4-BOOTSTRAP-CONFIG-TIMING-01 is resolved in the design: .NET 10 host lifecycle supports final test application configuration and test-service callbacks before an explicit-factory deferred container callback, which runs before provider construction. The plan rejects the previously failed top-level read and immediate callbacks, captures one immutable selection and allowlist snapshot, and reuses that selection after Build. Ordinary registrations remain once and early; ordinary mode has no October operational registration. Conditional October routes retain the same concrete certificate verifier, with only its authenticated-certificate source replaceable in controlled tests. Earlier P-18.4-01–04 findings remain resolved. Architecture classification remains required; this timing correction adds no Worker tool, Scan strategy, PRD change, Story 18.1 duplication or resource permission. Existing approvals remain semantically applicable subject to root-owned rebinding. Read-only SpecKit prerequisites passed; deterministic plan validation returned no errors, workflow validation reported no errors, and scoped diff check was clean. Source inspection establishes feasibility, not corrected-host GREEN: the actual WebApplicationFactory Program-host proof and later owned-resource qualification remain mandatory."
